## resolveViewingSystemInputs must resolve "fov" through the same
## dictionary Projection's own parameter list did: Declare redeclares
## "fov" before Projection sets it to 30, and RiWorldBegin has to see
## that value, not silently default to 90.
Display "declaredfov.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 100 100 1
Declare "fov" "float"
Projection "perspective" "fov" [30]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [1.0]
Sides 2
Color [1 1 1]
Surface "matte" "Ka" [1.0] "Kd" [0.0]
Polygon "P" [-1 -1 0  1 -1 0  1 1 0  -1 1 0]
WorldEnd
